{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-175711",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $3$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x-3 & =7 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x-3+3 & =7+3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x+0 & =10 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, multiplying both sides by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x & =10 \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cancel{2}}x & =2\\cdot 10 \\\\ x & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
